{
  "id": "interrole-conflict",
  "term": "interrole conflict",
  "definition": "Interrole conflict is tension that arises when the demands of one life role interfere with another, especially between work and non-work or family roles. In this research context, it is described as bidirectional and multidimensional, including conflicts tied to time, strain, and behaviour flowing from work to family or from family to work.",
